11. INTERVIEW ONE-LINER
====================================================


"Factory Method is a creational pattern that defines an interface
for creating objects but allows subclasses to decide which concrete
class should be instantiated. It reduces coupling and follows the
Open/Closed Principle."


====================================================
12. MEMORY TRICK
====================================================


Remember:


Client → Factory → Product


NOT:


Client → if-else → Concrete Object ❌


====================================================
13. KEY INTERVIEW POINTS
====================================================


Q: Why not create objects directly?

Answer:

"Direct creation couples the client with concrete classes.
Factory Method hides object creation and allows new types without
modifying existing client code."


Q: Why is it called Factory Method?

Answer:

"Because object creation is delegated to a factory method,
which subclasses can override to create different products."


Q: Is Simple Factory a Factory Method?

Answer:

"No. Simple Factory uses a single factory with if/switch logic.
Factory Method uses inheritance and separate factories."


